<title>UK: BCN Barclays prices $50 million eight-year bond.</title>
<headline>BCN Barclays prices $50 million eight-year bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond, announced earlier by lead manager BZW, has been priced.</p>
<p> BORROWER   BCN BARCLAYS BANCO DE INVESTIMENTO SA  </p>
<p> AMT    $50 MLN	 COUPON  ** 8.625     MATURITY   *18.NOV.04</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  100.133   PAY DATE    18.NOV.96</p>
<p> FULL FEES  1.0 PCT   REOFFER    99.883    SPREAD	+275 BP</p>
<p> MOODY	=	   LISTING    LUX	 PAY FREQ    =</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  =	   DENOMS (K) 10-50-100 SALE LIMITS US/UK</p>
<p> NEG PLG    YES	 CRS DEFLT  YES	 FORCE MAJ   IPMA (2)</p>
<p> GOV LAW    NEW YORK  HOME CTRY  =	   TAX PROVS   STD</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.75 PCT  SELL CONC  0.25 PCT  PRAECIPUUM  0.125 PCT</p>
<p> UNDERLYING GOVT BOND W/I THREE-YEAR U.S. TREASURY</p>
<p> NOTES	*PAR CALL AND PUT ON 18.NOV.99 AND 18.NOV.01</p>
<p>	     **STEPS UP TO 8.75 PCT AFTER THREE YEARS AND 8.875</p>
<p>		 PCT AFTER FIVE YEARS</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7718</p>
